A `{playbook}/{step}`-targeted rule renders on that step's `--step` surface, after the body, with
the step wording and no conflict clause; the playbook-targeted rule stays off this surface.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      core: {namespace: fx, path: ~/core-specs}
-- fixtures/home/core-specs/rule/0001-playbook-rule.md --
---
type: rule
title: Playbook rule
status: accepted
targets: [fx-rule-step]
brief: Playbook brief.
---
-- fixtures/home/core-specs/rule/0002-step-rule.md --
---
type: rule
title: Step rule
status: accepted
targets: [fx-rule-step/s1]
brief: Step brief.
---
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-step/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-rule-step
title: Rules
summary: Rule injection.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-step/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  s1: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-step/s1/prompt.md --
---
name: s1
summary: Only step.
detached: sonnet:medium
---

Step body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-rule-step --step s1
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Step body.

## Rules

The following 1 rule(s) apply to this step. Never silently violate one. Read a rule's record when its brief is not enough.

- **Step rule** — Step brief. [fx:rule/0002]({HOME}/core-specs/rule/0002-step-rule.md)
